summary:
I think this nicely captures why we can't have nice things, surreal number edition. You can go up countably many unit-length steps and down uncountably many unit-length steps, and still be infinitely large.
Quoting @JDHamkins
@gro_tsen Every surreal number has an Ord sequence converging to it from below, and in particular, the number 1 has such a sequence. This sequence will not be totally captured by your cover. I agree that it is indeed a little paradoxical. Think about how many unit-length intervals there are below omega. It's not just countably many, since you can still keep subtracting 1 for Ord many steps, while remaining infinite.

