The boundary between capabilities and safety is subtle, but that doesn’t conflict with it being rational to unilaterally stop stuff-that’s-just-obviously-capabilities-research.
Quoting @geoffreyirving
@phillip_isola The idea of needing to know the exact boundary is downstream of treating the problem as pure coordination. If you need to coordinate in a fair way to have coordination work at all, you have to know the boundary with some precision. If for sufficiently capabilities work unilateral stops are rational, the fact that someone else is uncertainty doesn’t matter.

